  "energy_arc": "Intro: Somber tanpura and sitar aochar unfolding Bhairav's ancient darkness; Mukhada 1: Crushing doom rhythm enters with full band weight; Manjha: Melodic descent into the mandra saptak over brooding chugs; Mukhada 2: Firm reassertion of the main hook with growing intensity; Antara: Sitar ascends into the taar register over rolling double-kick pulses; Takeover: Guitar seizes the mukhada with downtuned doom filth; Taan: Sitar unleashes a climactic virtuosic fury driven by relentless doom grooves; Mukhada 3: Triumphant final return of the gat hook; Outro: Sustained Sa chord ringing out into total doom decay.",
  "rhythm_section": {
    "reasoning": "Plan: Ground the arrangement in slow, crushing half-time doom power chords in Bhairav (E root). The home chord S holds across long spans, punctuated by heavy 8th-note chugs and 16th-note turnarounds. Section 1 (mukhada) establishes the recurring doom progression: S (8 beats) -> r (4 beats) -> d (2 beats) -> S (2 beats with turnaround), recurring identically in sections 3 and 7. Section 2 (manjha) moves through brooding lower-register contours: S (8 beats) ringing under the sitar's descent -> m (4 beats) -> P (4 beats) with sparse sustain, answering the sitar's rest at beats 12-16 with crushing stabs. Section 4 (antara) climbs an octave (+1) over P (4 beats) -> d (4 beats) -> N (4 beats) -> S (4 beats), sustaining ringing power chords under the sitar's taar register excursions. Section 5 is a takeover handled by the engine, so it is omitted. Section 6 (taan_long) provides an unyielding, relentless doom drive on a massive S pedal with heavy chugging momentum. Section 8 (outro) lets the low Sa dissolve into an apocalyptic vibrating decay.",
